WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.680
It’s an old adage that money makes the world
go round, and when you work for the SCP Foundation,

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.639
that same money can keep the world from ending.

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:13.491
Think for a second about the kind of absurd
bills that the SCP Foundation racks up: They

00:00:13.491 --> 00:00:17.590
need to pay for the upkeep on hundreds of
facilities while also paying for thousands

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:23.080
of employees - As well as stipends for the
families of the many, many, many members of

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.750
personnel who are killed in the line of duty.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.939
They also need to pay for the equipment required
to do their jobs - a lot of which they need

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:34.800
to develop themselves - as well as the expenses
of varied containment procedures for well

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.020
over 6000 different anomalies, each one requiring
its own unique treatment.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.600
And that’s not even factoring in the costs
of their various experiments, vehicles, weaponry,

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.330
and cover-up operations.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:51.760
To say the Foundation would need billions
upon billions of dollars to do what they do

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.630
is probably low-balling it.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.890
So today, we feel like asking the big question.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.370
How does the SCP Foundation make all this
money?

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.829
Because personally, we just don’t think
the bi-annual Foundation bake sale is going

00:01:04.829 --> 00:01:06.950
to cover the price tag on this thing.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:10.650
First, we’re going to explore the different
ways the Foundation probably brings in its

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:15.350
obscene budget through more traditional means,
but if you stick around to the end, we’ll

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.509
explore some of the much more strange and
exciting ways the Foundation can financially

00:01:19.509 --> 00:01:25.200
exploit its vast cache of anomalies, as well
as a way that you - that’s right, YOU!

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.200
- can help.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.549
So buckle up as we tackle the most terrifying
monster of all: Budgeting.

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:34.649
The most obvious means the Foundation has
of scraping up a little extra cash is its

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:36.649
cooperation with world governments.

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:41.859
Obviously, the SCP Foundation isn’t a puppet
of the United Nations like the GOC, it operates

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:46.350
with a high degree of autonomy that prevents
its work from ever being biased by certain

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.100
national or international interests.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:53.569
However, in order to do its work properly,
it does collaborate with various governments

00:01:53.569 --> 00:01:54.829
across the globe.

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:59.530
Naturally, as a result of this, it does receive
assisted funding from governments when combating

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:03.609
or containing anomalies that would present
a threat to their national security.

00:02:03.609 --> 00:02:08.140
Think of it as a classic “You scratch my
back, I scratch yours” situation.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.940
But seeing as people would notice every single
government on earth farming out billions of

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.310
dollars for seemingly no reason that the public
could account for, it’s clear that this

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:20.830
only accounts for one of the SCP Foundation’s
multiple income streams.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.410
Where else is all the money coming from?

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.800
Well, a phrase you’ve probably heard a lot
on the videos on this channel is “Front

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.810
Businesses.”

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.690
As any members of the Mafia in our audience
will already know, a front business is a seemingly

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:37.490
legitimate company used to hide the operations
of a more secretive or illicit business going

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.820
on behind the scenes.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:43.240
Typically, it’s a boon for organized crime
syndicates who need to justify the purchases

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.450
of certain personnel or equipment or launder
ill-gotten gains into clean, legitimate, taxable

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:49.690
revenue streams.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:55.120
Cause trust us, kids, the only three letters
scarier than SCP are IRS.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:00.200
The SCP Foundation makes use of a huge number
of front organizations to both hide its operations

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.150
and supplement its income.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.570
From chemical plants to office buildings to
local bakeries, it’s impossible to know

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:11.440
just how many normal industries technically
answer to the O5 Council high enough up the

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.440
chain.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:16.460
For all you know, you could already be an
employee of the SCP Foundation without even

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.150
being aware of it.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:22.110
Income generated by the various front companies
used by the Foundation are likely to make

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.120
up a good chunk of their budget.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.230
Another key factor in the Foundation’s profitability
is technology.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:32.060
Given that the Foundation has gathered some
of the greatest scientific and engineering

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.660
minds in the world to protect humanity from
anomalous forces, it goes without saying that

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:41.310
they create some incredible technology, which
may later trickle down into wider commercial

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.080
and civilian use.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.020
And before you start to say this is crazy,
it’s actually an incredibly common practice

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.710
with regular militaries all over the world.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:56.120
Duct tape, super glue, GPS, silly putty, EpiPens,
microwaves, and the internet were all made

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.750
possible by military advancements.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.690
And with the Foundation having technology
so advanced it puts even the most well-funded

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:06.770
militaries to shame, it’s sure to have some
similar lucrative patents floating around

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:07.770
out there.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:11.320
Not to mention the fact that the Foundation
has also reclaimed and repurposed anomalous

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:16.220
technology that surpasses even their own,
which may influence some incredibly profitable

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.660
consumer goods further down the line.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.419
Which is a nice segue to the next portion
of this video: Utilizing captured anomalies

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:25.289
for fun and profit!

00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:27.770
Well, mostly profit, in this case.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:31.919
This is the much more fun and theoretical
half of things, where we speculate on which

00:04:31.919 --> 00:04:37.060
SCPs would bring in the biggest bucks to fill
the coffers of the SCP Foundation.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.520
And of course, stick around to the end for
the most important money-making method of

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:41.520
all.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.669
It won’t be what you expect...

00:04:43.669 --> 00:04:44.819
First, SCP-096.

00:04:44.819 --> 00:04:48.560
We know what you’re thinking: How do we
monetize a mindless killing machine?

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.919
Simple, we stand someone in front of it and
make them look at its face, then position

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:56.810
096 onto a treadmill attached to a series
of powerful generators.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:01.380
Given that 096 literally never gets tired,
we will have invented a true perpetual motion

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:05.520
machine, and the energy generated by this
could replace the municipal power grid.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.789
That’s surely gotta be worth a few bucks,
right?

00:05:07.789 --> 00:05:10.599
United States Government, the Foundation awaits
your call.

00:05:10.599 --> 00:05:13.300
Okay, okay, let’s get a little more serious.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.029
Have you ever heard the expression “a penny
saved is a penny earned”?

00:05:17.029 --> 00:05:21.990
Because as previously discussed, one of the
major costs of the Foundation is labor.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:27.779
However, SCP-662 - The Butler’s Hand Bell
that summons the unfailingly loyal Mr. Deeds

00:05:27.779 --> 00:05:29.349
- could solve this issue.

00:05:29.349 --> 00:05:32.770
You may be thinking, “Sure, Mr. Deeds can
replace the labor of a couple of people, but

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:33.770
not that many!

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.259
He’s got physical limitations!”

00:05:35.259 --> 00:05:42.199
To which we would answer: What about SCP-662
put through SCP-914, The Clockworks, on Fine?

00:05:42.199 --> 00:05:46.889
We’d wager that this might lead to a bell
that summons an even more effective Mr. Deeds,

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:49.229
or better yet, multiple Mr. Deeds.

00:05:49.229 --> 00:05:53.139
You could only imagine the money the SCP Foundation
would save.

00:05:53.139 --> 00:05:55.620
Upon request, he can also manifest bricks
of pure gold.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.530
He’s a butler that literally pays for himself!

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:02.930
But enough about Mr. Deeds, let’s talk about
you: Are you happy?

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:03.930
Fulfilled?

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.580
Do you know why you’re here?

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:08.800
A lot of people struggle with finding a sense
of purpose in life.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.999
It can make it difficult to form and actualize
your goals.

00:06:11.999 --> 00:06:15.870
If only it was easy to know your greatest
desire, so you could finally get your life

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.930
together and start working on it.

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:21.229
Thankfully, the Foundation could help...For
a price.

00:06:21.229 --> 00:06:22.229
What?

00:06:22.229 --> 00:06:24.340
You can’t blame them for a little #hustle.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:28.909
With SCP-978, the Desire Camera, they could
help people figure out what their deepest

00:06:28.909 --> 00:06:29.909
desire is.

00:06:29.909 --> 00:06:33.909
But that’s not the only way to make money
from this anomalous device.

00:06:33.909 --> 00:06:38.259
By taking pictures of the rich and powerful,
and seeing if their desires are compromising,

00:06:38.259 --> 00:06:43.389
humiliating, or even illegal, you can quickly
solicit some very generous donations out of

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:47.960
them in exchange for keeping this juicy information
under wraps.

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:51.999
Podcasts are big these days - with incredibly
popular ones like the Joe Rogan Experience

00:06:51.999 --> 00:06:55.009
getting around eleven million downloads per
episode.

00:06:55.009 --> 00:06:58.110
People love hearing a compelling interview
or a good story.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:03.819
That’s why, to make a little money on the
side, we recommend the Foundation gives SCP-1867

00:07:03.819 --> 00:07:09.831
- a talkative telepathic sea slug who goes
by Lord Blackwood - his own podcast, where

00:07:09.831 --> 00:07:15.409
he would spin wild yarns, interview celebrity
guests, and perhaps even host chats with other

00:07:15.409 --> 00:07:20.979
interesting SCPs - All while the Foundation
cleans up on sweet, sweet podcast sponsorship

00:07:20.979 --> 00:07:21.979
revenue.

00:07:21.979 --> 00:07:26.009
What, are you telling us you wouldn’t tune
in?

00:07:26.009 --> 00:07:30.280
SCP-5094, Miss J’s Whiz Kid Schoolhouse,
could also be converted into expensive, over-the-counter

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.969
proprietary software.

00:07:31.969 --> 00:07:35.339
Think of the money that companies like Skillshare
and Masterclass rake in.

00:07:35.339 --> 00:07:39.839
Miss J could guarantee perfect learning through
her intensive courses, and once the word of

00:07:39.839 --> 00:07:44.520
her efficacy spreads, she might even replace
traditional higher education.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:45.800
And who would be the financial beneficiary?

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.830
The SCP Foundation.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:52.050
Then there’s SCP-2430, the Immortal Hitler
Clone.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:56.009
He’s unable to die, but feels pain at a
heightened degree of sensitivity than most

00:07:56.009 --> 00:07:58.059
normal people.

00:07:58.059 --> 00:08:00.999
He’s also...Hitler.

00:08:00.999 --> 00:08:05.229
And if the Foundation were able to go public
about the existence of this clone, they could

00:08:05.229 --> 00:08:09.840
take him out on tour across the globe, and
charge ten to fifteen bucks to punch him.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.249
People would be lining up to take a crack
at the ex-fuhrer, and the Foundation would,

00:08:13.249 --> 00:08:15.569
of course, be the sole financial beneficiaries.

00:08:15.569 --> 00:08:18.169
Now let’s talk about pizza.

00:08:18.169 --> 00:08:22.430
The most popular pizza chain in the United
States, as of this writing, is Domino’s,

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.740
with annual revenue of just over fourteen
billion dollars.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:30.339
What we’re wondering is: Why doesn’t the
SCP Foundation want a slice of that lucrative

00:08:30.339 --> 00:08:31.659
pizza pie?

00:08:31.659 --> 00:08:35.789
After all, they’re in possession of SCP-458,
the Never-Ending Pizza Box.

00:08:35.789 --> 00:08:40.349
With the help of this bad boy - capable of
producing nearly limitless quantities of pizza

00:08:40.349 --> 00:08:44.219
- they could surely start making a pretty
pepperoni penny.

00:08:44.219 --> 00:08:48.089
Lego products are also a multi-billion dollar
industry, pointing towards a clear desire

00:08:48.089 --> 00:08:53.990
in the market for those charming, colorful
blocks, and there’s no lego like SCP-387,

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.360
the Living Lego.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:59.339
Hardcore Lego enthusiasts all over the world
would pay through the nose to experience a

00:08:59.339 --> 00:09:04.170
product like this, and seeing as they’re
completely Safe - in both SCP nomenclature

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:08.000
and the more colloquial sense of the phrase
- the Foundation wouldn’t need to worry

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.400
about any lawsuits from concerned parents.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.240
They’d only need to worry about where to
put all their fancy new stacks of cold, hard

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.240
cash!

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.900
For those desiring a little escapism, the
Foundation could rent out SCP-1230, A Hero

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:21.990
Is Born.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:26.920
This book takes its readers on fabulous bespoke
dream adventures through fantastical lands,

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.820
and will surely give them an experience that
will last long after they finally wake up.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:36.080
In a world where people are willing to pay
top dollar for VR Experiences and creepy Facebook

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:41.320
Meta-Verses, being able to enter the wondrous
land of dreams is a welcome low-tech solution

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:46.259
that would still likely make the SCP Foundation
boatloads of new income.

00:09:46.259 --> 00:09:48.370
We live in a stressful world.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:52.610
Modern life has not only come with its wealth
of new personal issues, from work troubles

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.029
to the dating game.

00:09:54.029 --> 00:09:58.089
And connectivity has come at the cost of having
an ever-greater awareness of the troubles

00:09:58.089 --> 00:10:00.200
that plague the world at large.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:04.630
With costs making a lot of valuable therapy
and medications unavailable to many, it’s

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:07.770
no wonder that we’re undergoing a global
mental health crisis.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:12.980
But the Foundation has a solution: SCP-999.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:16.610
Spend long enough time with him, and he’ll
straight up cure everything from depression

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.089
to PTSD.

00:10:18.089 --> 00:10:22.270
People all over the world would pay top dollar
to achieve an immediate and effective cure

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:27.660
to all mental maladies that only takes a few
hours, and has no negative side effects.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.570
Like the ultimate therapy dog.

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:33.339
The Foundation would be rolling in the dough
from an opportunity like this.

00:10:33.339 --> 00:10:38.150
And of course, the most devious, ingenious,
and overall effective method that the SCP

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:42.370
Foundation could possibly use to make money
is creating YouTube channels that pretend

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:47.560
to just be sharing the fictional monsters
and entities of a made-up online fiction project.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:51.880
When, in fact, they’re actually secretly
leaking the highly classified secrets of their

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:56.260
own organization, while selling adorable,
high-quality merchandise of some of their

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:58.550
most lovable and iconic creatures.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:01.389
We can’t think of any method more valuable
than that.

00:11:01.389 --> 00:11:05.760
Anyway, on a completely different note, did
you know you can get your very own adorable

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.360
SCP-999 plushie, pictured here looking cute
as all heck?

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:14.980
All you need to do is visit www.scpswag.com,
and you can have your very own Tickle Monster

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.360
to hug any time you please!

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.910
And of course, if there are any other highly
profitable anomalies you’d like to see in

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:24.819
plush form, do take the time to make your
suggestions heard down in the comments.

00:11:24.819 --> 00:11:28.139
Now, if you’ll excuse us, we need to head
off.

00:11:28.139 --> 00:11:30.649
After all, time is money.

00:11:30.649 --> 00:11:35.940
Now go check out “SCP Foundation Boss - The
Administrator Explained” and “Top 8 SCP

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:40.190
Objects You Actually Want” for more esoteric
questions about the inner workings of the

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:42.260
SCP Foundation and its anomalies!

